From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:20:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: add the CX power domain to DISPCC

The same as 26d7b23caa4b ("arm64: dts: qcom: agatti: Add missing CX power
domain to DISPCC") for SM6115: put DISPCC on VDD_CX, so the genpd
performance votes of its MDSS GDSC reach the CX rail. DISPCC takes runtime
PM with it (our 0152), so the vote goes away when no display clock is in
use. After 1172 (both edit the DISPCC node).

Not posted. Not HW-tested.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
index bdab343bd4a5..10b9f8422ba1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
@@ -2188,6 +2188,7 @@ dispcc: clock-controller@5f00000 {
 				 <&mdss_dsi0_phy DSI_PIXEL_PLL_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_DISP_GPLL0_DIV_CLK_SRC>,
 				 <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_XO_A_CLK_SRC>;
+			power-domains = <&rpmpd SM6115_VDDCX>;
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
-- 
